{"id":"922132b2011d6694","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-df-axiom.md","title":"Axiom","display":"df-axiom — Axiom","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-axiom","aliases":["58-df-axiom","Axiom"],"display":"df-axiom — Axiom","depends_on":["[[58-df-theory]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-axiom"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-axiom</span><span>Axiom</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-axiom — Axiom"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"58-df-theory\">58-df-theory</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma,T,\\phi\\in V\">\\(\\Sigma,T,\\phi\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\">\\(\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\)</span> (theory over the signature <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma\">\\(\\Sigma\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"90ce6acf0c65af45\" href=\"?note=90ce6acf0c65af45\" title=\"58-df-theory\">58-df-theory</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Axiom}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Axiom}_S\\)</span> (axiom-membership predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}axiom} \\vdash \\mathrm{Axiom}_S(\\phi,T,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\phi\\in T\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}axiom} \\vdash \\mathrm{Axiom}_S(\\phi,T,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\phi\\in T\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>An axiom of a presented theory is a designated sentence of that theory; it need not be self-evident or unprovable from the other axioms.</li>\n<li>Satisfiability and syntactic consistency are separate definitions, while the completeness and incompleteness theorems are theorem-level statements.</li>\n<li>Axiom schemata specify families of axioms, such as separation and replacement in ZFC.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Kunen, Set Theory</li>\n<li>Mendelson, Introduction to Mathematical Logic</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-theory","status":"resolved","id":"90ce6acf0c65af45","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-theory]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-theory","status":"resolved","id":"90ce6acf0c65af45","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)$ (theory over the signature $\\Sigma$, see [[58-df-theory]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Sigma,T,\\phi\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)","display":false},{"tex":"\\Sigma","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Axiom}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}axiom} \\vdash \\mathrm{Axiom}_S(\\phi,T,\\Sigma)\\leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Theory}(T,\\Sigma)\\land\\phi\\in T","display":true}],"bytes":1013,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-159","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-df-axiom.md|58-df-axiom]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["90ce6acf0c65af45"]}